# ⚡ NEXT.JS 15 & TAILWIND CSS ARCHITECTURE

## 1. Directory Structure Conventions
```
src/
├── app/                  # Next.js 15 App Router
│   ├── layout.tsx        # Root layout with HTML/Body and Providers
│   ├── page.tsx          # Home page
│   ├── globals.css       # Tailwind & CSS variable declarations
│   └── api/              # Route handlers (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
├── components/
│   ├── ui/               # Reusable primitive UI (button, card, badge, dialog)
│   ├── layout/           # Header, footer, sidebar, navigation
│   └── [feature]/        # Feature-scoped components (e.g., catalog, auth, cart)
├── lib/                  # Utility functions (cn, formatters, client instances)
├── types/                # Global TypeScript declarations and domain types
└── hooks/                # Custom React hooks (prefixed with `use`)
```

## 2. Next.js 15 App Router Rules
- **Route Handlers**: Use `NextRequest` and `NextResponse` from `next/server`.
- **Metadata**: Define `export const metadata: Metadata = { ... }` or `generateMetadata` for dynamic pages.
- **Image Optimization**: Always use `next/image` with explicit `width`, `height`, and `alt`.
- **Navigation**: Always use `next/link` for internal links.

## 3. Tailwind CSS & shadcn/ui Standards
- UI primitives should follow shadcn/ui patterns using `cva` (class-variance-authority).
- Colors are referenced via CSS variables: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `border-border`.
- Responsive breakpoints:
  - `sm:` (640px)
  - `md:` (768px)
  - `lg:` (1024px)
  - `xl:` (1280px)
- Never mix raw inline CSS `style={{ ... }}` when Tailwind utility classes can achieve the same result.

## 4. State Management
- Prefer URL query parameters (`searchParams`) for filter, pagination, and sorting state.
- Use React Context only for global UI states (e.g. theme, active modal).
- Keep state local to components whenever possible.
